USOS 3.1.2-usos7 patch 8/8 (2026-10-15): APM power-off for Windows 9x and other APM callers; SeaBIOS debug output on the serial port

Windows 98 SE / ME on the ASRock X470 (CSM off, CSMWrap) end at "It's now
safe to turn off your computer" instead of powering off. Two holes in the
APM 5307h (BX=0001h, CX=0003h) power-off of CSMWrap 3.1.2:
1. From the 16-bit and 32-bit protected-mode APM interfaces (Windows 9x
   VPOWERD connects the 32-bit one), apm_shutdown() called
   bios_proxy_reset(), which scans the F-segment with real-mode segment
   loads (find_bios_proxy -> GET_FARVAR -> mov %es) = #GP in protected
   mode.
2. The fallback wrote 0x2000 (SLP_EN, SLP_TYP 0) to PM1a_CNT. SLP_TYP 0 is
   S5 on QEMU's PIIX4/ICH9 only; the X470 DSDT has Name(_S5, {5,0,0,0}),
   so the right write there is 0x3400.

Own code from the APM 1.2 specification (5303h, 5307h) and the ACPI
specification (6.x: 4.8.3.2 PM1 control registers, 5.2.9 FADT, 5.4 AML
encoding, 7.4.2 \_Sx states):
- fw/usos_s5.h: finds Name(_S5, Package(){a, b, ...}) in the DSDT (else an
  SSDT) without an interpreter; find_acpi_features() stores SLP_TYPa/b,
  PM1b_CNT, the PM timer and SMI_CMD/ACPI_ENABLE (X_ GAS fallbacks).
- stacks.c usos_proxy_reset_timed(): the helper-core ResetSystem request
  through the existing mailbox, written with %es = F000h in real/V86 mode
  and through %gs (the APM data segment, based at the F-segment) from the
  32-bit PM interface; 2 s timeout. The helper-core loop is unchanged.
- apm.c: order 1. UEFI ResetSystem(EfiResetShutdown) on the helper core
  (INT 15h and 32-bit PM callers), 2. direct S5 write (SLP_TYP from \_S5,
  PM1a and PM1b, then SLP_EN), 3. still on after 2 s with SCI_EN = 0: ACPI
  mode on via SMI_CMD and S5 again, 4. still on: the call fails with
  AH=60h instead of halting. The 16-bit PM interface goes straight to 2.
  _PTS(5) is not run (no AML interpreter). Result bytes for INT 15h
  callers at BDA 4FCh-4FFh, "USOS APMOFF:" debug lines.
- serialio.c/csm.c/csmwrap.c/LegacyBios.h: CsmwrapFlags bit 0x02 and
  CsmwrapSerialPort; with csmwrap.ini serial = true SeaBIOS dprintf level 1
  goes to that port (it had no output in this build: no DEBUG_SERIAL).
- scripts/layoutrom.py: the minimum F-segment allocation zone goes from
  2048 to 6144 bytes. With this patch the code no longer leaves room in
  the F-segment, the layout falls back to that minimum, and 2048 bytes
  lost AHCI port 1 in QEMU (SMBIOS + MP table copies + per-port blocks).

Applies on top of patches 0001-0007 to CSMWrap 3.1.2 (808ac8e) with its
seabios submodule (578d260b), patch -p1 from the top of the tree. Part of
CSMWrap 3.1.2-usos7, a MODIFIED version made by the USOS project
(LGPL-2.1 / SeaBIOS LGPLv3).

